  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nSurface high pressure continues to build across the Ohio Valley from \nthe northwest today. Dry conditions and below average temperatures \npersist with highs in the 70s to near 80. \n\nThe surface high shifts east of the region this weekend which will \nallow warmer temperatures and higher dew points to move back into the\narea from the south. Shower and thunderstorms chances return along with\nthe summer like conditions. Upper level shortwave troughs moving \nthrough the northwesterly flow aloft could lead to periods of greater\nstorm coverage at times. One potential period for more storm \nactivity is Monday evening and Monday night. Instability may end up \noverlapping with strong shear when a potential cluster of storms or \nMCS sinks into the Ohio Valley from the northwest. Confidence is \nlow regarding the details at this time frame, but there is a signal\nfor convective activity somewhere in the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley\nlate Monday.",
